  "prefLabel": "Rev 701.06 Furnishings and accommodations",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rev 701.06 “Furnishings and accommodations” means the personal property or facilities used or provided for use in conjunction with the renting of sleeping accommodations, such as but not limited to, the use of:\n\n(a) Pools, beaches, or other sites associated with swimming or boating;\n\n(b) In-room television or radio;\n\n(c) Equipment associated with exercise, health, or athletic activities; or\n\n(d) Restaurants, lounges, or other facilities providing any forms of entertainment.\n\nSource. #2205, eff 12-12-82; ss by #2504, eff 10-12-83; ss by #3181, eff 1-22-86; ss by #4061, eff 5-29-86; ss by #5399, eff 5-21-92 (See Revision Note at part heading for Rev 701); ss by #6750, eff 5-19-98, EXPIRED: 5-19-06\n\nNew. #8653, eff 6-8-06; ss by #10714, eff 11-7-14 (from Rev 701.07); ss by #14105, eff 10-29-24, EXPIRES: 10-29-34 (formerly Rev 701.09)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/rev700.html"
